{
  "_note": "Profession-neutral occupational taxonomy. This is DATA, not code: every family is processed by the same uniform code path in src/profile/roleFamilies.js, so adding a field means editing this file and nothing else. It answers two questions with one table: (1) which families does THIS CANDIDATE belong to (from their own target roles, background roles and skills), and (2) which family does THIS POSTING TITLE belong to. A posting is only rejected when its family is confidently known AND shares nothing with the candidate's. That test is symmetric — no family is privileged, and 'not data engineering' is not a rejection reason.",
  "_fields": {
    "label": "Human-readable family name, used in dashboard explanations.",
    "roles": "Whole role phrases. The strongest signal: a match here is worth `roleWeight`.",
    "heads": "Role nouns this family uses as the head of a title ('engineer', 'nurse', 'manager'). Weak on their own — many families share them.",
    "domain": "Subject-matter words that modify a head noun ('data', 'regulatory', 'brand'). This is what actually separates families.",
    "skills": "Tools, methods, credentials and systems. Used to place a CANDIDATE, rarely a title."
  },
  "weights": {
    "role": 6,
    "domain": 3,
    "skill": 2,
    "head": 1
  },
